<title>CANADA: Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Suncor raises Canada posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suncor Energy Inc said on Tuesday it raised the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$4.00/cubic metre or C$0.64/barrel, to C$163.00/cubic metre or C$25.91/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$153.00/cubic metre, or C$24.33/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$138.00/cubic metre, or C$21.94/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
